# What no image needs. This is a deny-list on purpose.
#
# Two Dockerfiles build from this context:
#   * graph-http/Dockerfile and graph-web/Dockerfile (used by docker-compose.yml) do `COPY . .` and run Maven
#     inside the builder stage, so they need the source tree;
#   * the root Dockerfile (used by tools/release-1.0.sh) copies the staged jar from dist/, which is why dist/
#     must stay in the context.
#
# The first version of this file was an allow-list (`*` then `!Dockerfile !dist/`), which broke both compose
# builds: an ignore file that describes one build's needs while three builds share it is a build that works
# until someone else runs the other command. An earlier version excluded `**/target` *and* the root Dockerfile
# copied from `graph-http/target/`, which failed with "no such file or directory" - the artifact a build needs
# must not be ignored, and the release build stages its jar outside target/ for exactly that reason.
.git
.gitattributes
.idea
.sessions
.logs
.rocksdb
.datasets
**/target
**/node_modules
*.log
*.iml
